/-
  * Examples.RwxFlagNs.SourceMemImage — the SOURCE binary's ELF snapshot

  SNAPSHOT OUTPUT — the bytes below are what `elf-snapshot` produced for
  this binary, do not hand-edit them.  The hand-written parts are the note
  below and the sanity section at the end.

  The image is ONE LOAD segment, `rwx`, at `0x10000`, 4 KiB: the ELF
  headers, `.text` and the writable data all share it (built through
  `source/rwx.lds`, which is why the example exists).  Inside the segment,

  - `0x000 .. 0x078`  ELF header, program header table, and `_start`'s
    opening `auipc gp, 0x1` is at `0x078` itself;
  - `0x078 .. 0x0e4`  `.text` — the eighteen instructions the source
    derivation steps through.  This is the range `stext_lo`/`stext_hi`
    in `RwxFlagNsDefs.lean` states the `mem_clear` frame invariant over;
  - `0x0e4 .. 0x1000` `.data`/`.bss` — the `flag` byte at `0x100e4` (its
    initial value 7), musl's `__environ` slot at `0x100e8` — then the
    page's zero fill.

  HOW THE BYTES GET HERE.  Lean has no build-time file inclusion, so the
  4096 bytes are written out below as their lowercase hex, in chunks of
  8 bytes, four chunks (32 bytes) to a source line with the line's byte
  offset in a comment — the layout `xxd -c 32` prints.  Chunk boundaries
  carry no memory semantics (`segment_byte_at` is boundary-transparent by
  construction), so this is the same `seg_bytes` payload the model
  documents, spelled across more than one chunk.  The choice of an 8-byte
  chunk is not cosmetic: kernel reduction of the hex decoder is quadratic
  in the chunk length, so the payload-visible proofs
  (`RwxFlagNsDefs.source_wseg` and the fetch facts) are the difference
  between seconds and hours.  The empty diff is real: a `decide` over one
  8 KiB chunk does not terminate in practice.
-/
import LinuxSem.LinuxProcessSem.MemImageType

/- The byte-level checks at the end go through the model's own hex
   decoder (`segment_read_bytes`). -/
import LinuxSem.LinuxProcessSem.RiscvSemantics

/- `autoImplicit` is off: a bare field name in a statement would
   otherwise become an implicitly bound variable, i.e. a weakened claim
   rather than a compile error. -/
set_option autoImplicit false

/- The byte-level checks reduce the model's hex decoder; that is deeper
   than the default `decide` recursion budget.  A resource knob, not a
   proof step. -/
set_option maxRecDepth 40000

namespace LinuxSem.Examples.RwxFlagNs

namespace SourceMemImage

open LinuxSem.LinuxProcessSem.MemImageType
open LinuxSem.LinuxProcessSem.RiscvSemantics

